&lt;p&gt;Yahoo identifies several possible warning signs of account compromise, including unexpected login locations, changed account information, missing emails, and messages being sent without the user's knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should also inspect:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Email filters&lt;br&gt;
• Auto-forwarding settings&lt;br&gt;
• Reply-to addresses&lt;br&gt;
• Signatures&lt;br&gt;
• Automatic responses&lt;br&gt;
• Blocked addresses&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unexpected changes can indicate unauthorized account access.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What to Do If an Account Is Compromised&lt;br&gt;
If a Yahoo Account appears compromised, users should act promptly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recommended actions include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Change the password.&lt;br&gt;
Remove unfamiliar app passwords.&lt;br&gt;
Review recovery information.&lt;br&gt;
Check email settings.&lt;br&gt;
Review recent activity.&lt;br&gt;
Confirm 2FA settings.&lt;br&gt;
Secure the device.&lt;br&gt;
Follow Yahoo's official account-recovery guidance.&lt;br&gt;
Yahoo recommends these types of steps when an account may have been compromised.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Old Yahoo Accounts and Security Considerations&lt;br&gt;
An older Yahoo Account is not automatically safer or more valuable simply because it has existed for a long time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Account security depends on factors such as:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Password strength&lt;br&gt;
• 2FA configuration&lt;br&gt;
• Recovery information&lt;br&gt;
• Device security&lt;br&gt;
• Recent account activity&lt;br&gt;
• Connected applications&lt;br&gt;
• User behavior&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Account age by itself should not be considered a security feature.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Risks of Previously Controlled or Transferred Accounts&lt;br&gt;
Users may encounter offers involving previously used Yahoo Accounts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Such accounts can create risks related to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Ownership&lt;br&gt;
• Previous recovery information&lt;br&gt;
• Privacy&lt;br&gt;
• Account history&lt;br&gt;
• Security settings&lt;br&gt;
• Access recovery&lt;br&gt;
• Unknown connected services&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Even if 2FA is enabled, these issues may remain.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For legitimate personal or professional use, maintaining an account under your own control is the safer approach.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Long-Term Yahoo Account Maintenance&lt;br&gt;
A regular maintenance routine can help users keep their account secure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Monthly Security Review&lt;br&gt;
Check:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Recent sign-in activity&lt;br&gt;
• Recovery information&lt;br&gt;
• 2FA methods&lt;br&gt;
• App passwords&lt;br&gt;
• Connected services&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Regular Inbox Review&lt;br&gt;
Clean:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Unnecessary messages&lt;br&gt;
• Old notifications&lt;br&gt;
• Unwanted subscriptions&lt;br&gt;
• Duplicate information&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Device Review&lt;br&gt;
Make sure:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Devices are updated&lt;br&gt;
• Screen locks are enabled&lt;br&gt;
• Security software is current&lt;br&gt;
• Unknown applications are removed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo Account Security Checklist&lt;br&gt;
Password&lt;br&gt;
Use a strong password.&lt;br&gt;
Keep it unique.&lt;br&gt;
Avoid password reuse.&lt;br&gt;
2FA&lt;br&gt;
Enable 2-step verification.&lt;br&gt;
Protect the authentication method.&lt;br&gt;
Keep recovery options available.&lt;br&gt;
Privacy&lt;br&gt;
Protect personal information.&lt;br&gt;
Review account settings.&lt;br&gt;
Check connected services.&lt;br&gt;
App Passwords&lt;br&gt;
Remove unknown app passwords.&lt;br&gt;
Create them only when needed.&lt;br&gt;
Never share them publicly.&lt;br&gt;
Email Safety&lt;br&gt;
Avoid suspicious links.&lt;br&gt;
Be careful with attachments.&lt;br&gt;
Never share verification codes.&lt;br&gt;
Frequently Asked Questions&lt;br&gt;
What is a Yahoo Account with 2FA?&lt;br&gt;
It is a Yahoo Account protected by an additional authentication step beyond the normal password.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Does 2FA guarantee complete security?&lt;br&gt;
No. 2FA provides an important additional layer, but users must also protect their passwords, devices, recovery information, and authentication methods.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can Yahoo use an authenticator app for 2FA?&lt;br&gt;
Yes. Yahoo supports authenticator-app verification for eligible account configurations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Does Yahoo support security keys?&lt;br&gt;
Yes. Yahoo provides security-key support as an available authentication method.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Are app passwords the same as the main Yahoo password?&lt;br&gt;
No. App passwords are separate credentials intended for supported third-party applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Is an old Yahoo Account automatically better?&lt;br&gt;
No. Account age does not guarantee security, reliability, ownership, or quality.&lt;/p&gt;

