&lt;p&gt;Authentication Methods&lt;br&gt;
Google supports several modern authentication approaches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Google Prompts&lt;br&gt;
A Google prompt can allow a user to confirm a login through a trusted device.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should never approve an unexpected login request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Authenticator Applications&lt;br&gt;
Authenticator applications can generate temporary verification codes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should keep the device containing the authenticator application secure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Security Keys&lt;br&gt;
Security keys provide a physical authentication method.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;They can provide strong protection against certain types of phishing and unauthorized access.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Passkeys&lt;br&gt;
Passkeys are a modern authentication technology designed to provide secure sign-in without relying solely on traditional passwords.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should maintain appropriate backup and recovery options when configuring modern authentication methods.&lt;/p&gt;

